The UK median gross annual salary for marketing and commercial managers was £50,589 in 2025, up 6.7% on 2024, according to the Office for National Statistics. This is a provisional 2025 figure from the Annual Survey of Hours and Earnings, published 23 October 2025. The 2026 edition is scheduled for 22 October 2026 and has not yet been published, so every figure on this page is the most recent official data available as of 24 September 2026.

ASHE is the UK government's primary source for pay by occupation. It samples employee jobs through PAYE records, not job adverts or self-reported surveys. It does not cover the self-employed, so freelance and consultant day rates sit outside every figure below.

## What do marketing managers and directors earn in the UK? {% #marketing-managers %}

ASHE groups marketing roles by Standard Occupational Classification 2020 (SOC 2020) unit group. The table below shows gross annual pay for full-time and part-time employees combined, UK-wide, 2025 provisional.

| Occupation (SOC 2020) | Jobs (000s) | Median | Mean | 25th percentile | 75th percentile |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Marketing, sales and advertising directors (1132) | 216 | £90,000 | £108,331 | £60,138 | £131,906 |
| Marketing and commercial managers (2432) | 100 | £50,589 | £58,333 | £37,860 | £67,702 |
| All UK employees | 24,897 | £32,890 | £40,269 | £22,060 | £48,283 |

Both marketing occupations sit well above the UK all-employee median. Directors earn roughly 2.7 times the UK median at the midpoint; managers earn around 1.5 times it. The gap between the 25th and 75th percentile is wide for both groups, which means a single average understates how much marketing pay varies by seniority, sector and company size within the same job title.

SOC 1132 covers sales directors alongside marketing and advertising directors, so this unit group is not marketing-only. Treat the £90,000 median as a broader commercial-leadership figure, not a marketing-director-specific one.

{% stats %}
{% stat value="£50,589" label="UK median gross annual salary for marketing and commercial managers, 2025 provisional" source="ONS ASHE 2025 provisional, Table 14" /%}
{% stat value="£90,000" label="UK median gross annual salary for marketing, sales and advertising directors, 2025 provisional" source="ONS ASHE 2025 provisional, Table 14" /%}
{% /stats %}

## How do marketing salaries vary by region? {% #regional-pay %}

ASHE Table 15 breaks pay down by workplace region. Table 15 covers Great Britain only; Northern Ireland runs a separate earnings survey and is not included in these rows. Several regional cells for narrow occupation codes are suppressed for quality reasons (marked "x" below), usually because the regional sample is too small for a reliable estimate.

| Region | Marketing and commercial managers (2432), median | Marketing associate professionals (3554), median |
|---|---|---|
| London | £59,163 | £35,000 |
| South East | £49,265 | £30,363 |
| East | £62,752 | £30,127 |
| South West | £41,418 | £27,575 |
| West Midlands | £51,700 | £29,033 |
| Yorkshire and The Humber | suppressed | £28,887 |
| North West | £47,843 | £28,013 |
| Wales | £50,308 | £26,525 |
| North East | suppressed | suppressed |
| East Midlands | suppressed | £30,148 |
| Scotland | suppressed | suppressed |

London's median for marketing associate professionals is £35,000, around 25% above the North West's £28,013. The gap is smaller for the more senior 2432 group where regional samples are thinner and comparisons are less reliable. Where a region shows "suppressed," ONS has withheld the estimate because too few sampled jobs fall in that region-occupation combination to be reliable, not because pay there is unusually high or low.

## How much do people working in SEO earn in the UK? {% #seo-pay %}

SOC 2020 has no separate "SEO" occupation. SEO roles are coded within broader occupations depending on seniority: most in-house SEO executives and specialists fall under marketing associate professionals (SOC 3554), while SEO managers and heads of SEO are more likely to be coded under marketing and commercial managers (SOC 2432) above. Any "SEO salary UK" figure you see quoted elsewhere is either a job-board average, drawn from a smaller employer survey, or an approximation using one of these broader ASHE groups. None of the published ASHE tables isolate SEO specifically.

Marketing associate professionals, UK-wide, 2025 provisional: median £30,479, mean £35,886, up 5.2% on 2024. The middle half of this group earns between £24,032 (25th percentile) and £39,205 (75th percentile). The 10th percentile sits at £12,925, which reflects part-time and junior entry-level roles pulling the lower end down.

| Percentile | Marketing associate professionals (3554) |
|---|---|
| 10th | £12,925 |
| 25th | £24,032 |
| Median | £30,479 |
| 75th | £39,205 |
| 90th | suppressed |

This is a broader marketing-associate-professional figure, not an SEO-specific one. Treat it as the closest official proxy, not a direct measurement.

{% stats %}
{% stat value="£30,479" label="UK median gross annual salary for marketing associate professionals, the closest SOC 2020 proxy for SEO executive and specialist roles, 2025 provisional" source="ONS ASHE 2025 provisional, Table 14" /%}
{% /stats %}

## How much do PR and advertising professionals earn? {% #pr-advertising-pay %}

Public relations sits in its own SOC 2020 codes, separate from marketing. Public relations professionals had a median of £36,336 in 2025, up 5.6% on 2024. Public relations and communications directors had a median of £72,020, down 2.4% on 2024, though this unit group's small UK sample means several of its percentile cells are suppressed and the year-on-year change should be read with more caution than the larger occupations above.

| Occupation (SOC 2020) | Jobs (000s) | Median | Mean |
|---|---|---|---|
| Public relations and communications directors (1133) | suppressed | £72,020 | £80,842 |
| Public relations professionals (2493) | 39 | £36,336 | £37,761 |
| Advertising accounts managers and creative directors (2494) | 31 | £46,356 | £52,936 |

## What do self-employed SEO consultants and freelancers charge? {% #self-employed %}

ASHE only samples employee jobs through PAYE records. It excludes the self-employed entirely, so none of the figures above tell you what a freelance SEO consultant, sole trader or contractor charges. For published UK consultant pricing, hourly rates, day rates and retainer ranges, see [how much does an SEO consultant charge in the UK](/blog/how-much-does-an-seo-consultant-charge-uk/). This page does not attempt to estimate consultant day rates from ASHE data, because the two populations, employees and the self-employed, are not comparable.

If you are budgeting for in-house marketing hires against agency or consultant costs, a fixed-fee [SEO audit](/services/paid-seo-audit/) can show where an outside specialist adds more value than an internal hire at these salary levels, and where the reverse is true.

## What does ASHE not measure? {% #methodology %}

ASHE draws its sample from HM Revenue and Customs PAYE records, so every figure on this page describes employee jobs, not self-employment income, freelance rates, bonuses paid outside the survey reference period, or equity and share-based pay. The 2025 edition used here is provisional; ONS revises it into a "2025 revised" release alongside the 2026 provisional figures, expected 22 October 2026.

Percentile and mean cells marked "suppressed" or "x" in the tables above are withheld by ONS because the underlying sample size or coefficient of variation does not meet its quality threshold. This is common for narrow four-digit occupation codes split further by region, and it is a data-quality limit, not a missing zero. Do not treat a suppressed cell as £0 or interpolate a number for it.

SOC 2020 unit groups are functional job classifications, not company-specific titles. A "digital marketing executive," "SEO specialist" or "content marketing manager" job title can be coded to marketing associate professionals (3554), and a "head of marketing," "marketing director" or "commercial director" can be coded to either marketing and commercial managers (2432) or marketing, sales and advertising directors (1132), depending on seniority and scope. This page reports the SOC unit group, not individual job titles, because ASHE does not publish by job title.

All figures are gross annual pay for full-time and part-time employee jobs combined, United Kingdom, unless a table states otherwise. Source: Office for National Statistics, Annual Survey of Hours and Earnings 2025 provisional and 2024 revised results, Table 14 (occupation, four-digit SOC 2020) and Table 15 (region by occupation, four-digit SOC 2020), published 23 October 2025. Checked 24 September 2026.

